  "id": "tax.us.2025.rule.form1040-line25b",
  "notes": "Form 1040 line 25b: 'Add the amounts shown as federal income tax withheld' on Forms 1099-INT, 1099-DIV, 1099-R box 4, 1099-G box 4 and SSA-1099 box 6 (i1040gi-2025 l.2559-2576). Each document's own subtotal rule is pinned and added here, one addend per document, so the explanation walk reaches each one. Form 1099-K box 4 stays outside the class (SC-R1; a nonzero 1099-K box 4 is refused by the 1099-K loss-reason rule). v4 published only when a family's withholding count was at least its income count. v5 replaces that comparison with require_paired: every current row of the family's income fact types has a current withholding row on the same statement key. The income types are 1099-INT boxes 1, 3, 8 and 10; 1099-DIV boxes 1a, 2a and 12; 1099-R IRA box 1; 1099-G box 1; SSA-1099 box 5. Each family's income closure stays inside that family's arm, and the five withholding closures stay outside. A missing withholding row blocks DEPENDENCY_ABSENT naming that family's withholding fact (the first family, in the order listed, that is short). A $0 row counts because the row exists. A withholding row with no income row is not a failure. The value, requires, pins, blocked, citations, and scope are unchanged from v4.",
